    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "summary",
      "x": -23.86016845703125,
      "y": 580.171875,
      "width": 1225.3299560546875,
      "height": 60,
      "text": "SELECT → duplicates (broken)     |     FOR UPDATE → correct but serialized (slow)     |     FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED → correct + parallel (ours)\n\nThis is the foundation: Postgres row-level locking gives us work queue semantics with ACID guarantees. No broker, no distributed lock, no leader.",
      "originalText": "SELECT → duplicates (broken)     |     FOR UPDATE → correct but serialized (slow)     |     FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED → correct + parallel (ours)\n\nThis is the foundation: Postgres row-level locking gives us work queue semantics with ACID guarantees. No broker, no distributed lock, no leader.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
